<title>USA: Paramount names vice chairman of pictures.</title>
<headline>Paramount names vice chairman of pictures.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Viacom Inc's Paramount Pictures said Robert Friedman was appointed vice chairman of the motion picture group.</p>
<p>Friedman, who will assume his duties no later than February 1, succeeding Barry London, who resigned last week and has entered into a production deal with the studio.</p>
<p>Friedman joins Paramount after a distinguished 26-year career at Time Warner Inc's Warner Brothers.</p>
<p>Since 1989, he served as president of worldwide advertising and publicity at Warner Brothers. Before that, he served as senior vice president of advertising and publicity. He began his mailroom at Warner Brothers in September 1970.</p>
